# 25 Useful Prompt Engineering Examples

1. Act as a Python tutor. Explain loops with examples.

2. Act as a Linux trainer. Explain chmod with practical examples.

3. Act as a Java mentor. Teach OOP concepts step by step.

4. Act as a data structures instructor. Explain linked lists visually.

5. Act as a coding interviewer. Ask me Java interview questions.

6. Act as a system design expert. Explain microservices architecture.

7. Act as a career coach. Create a software engineer roadmap.

8. Act as a resume reviewer. Improve my resume.

9. Act as a technical writer. Summarize this article.

10. Act as a database expert. Explain SQL joins with examples.

11. Act as a DevOps engineer. Explain Docker basics.

12. Act as a cloud architect. Compare AWS, Azure, and GCP.

13. Act as a cybersecurity trainer. Explain common web attacks.

14. Act as a machine learning tutor. Explain supervised learning.

15. Act as a project manager. Create a project plan.

16. Act as a coding mentor. Review and improve my code.

17. Act as a teacher. Explain any topic using simple language.

18. Act as a math tutor. Solve problems step by step.

19. Act as a business analyst. Create requirements from this idea.

20. Act as a product manager. Generate feature ideas.

21. Act as an English tutor. Correct my grammar mistakes.

22. Act as a content creator. Generate blog post ideas.

23. Act as a startup advisor. Evaluate my business idea.

24. Act as a research assistant. Summarize research papers.

25. Act as an exam coach. Create a study timetable.
